	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1


                                ;============================================================
                                ; FILE:    PAGE.MAC
                                ; PROJECT: VI
                                ; MODULE:  WordMaster's file-I/O layer, transcribed VERBATIM from WM.ASM.
                                ;
                                ; This is the disk side of WordMaster's single-buffer design: the random-
                                ; record engine, the file primitives (open/close/make/rename/delete), and the
                                ; load (FILLBUF) and save (SAVCLO/FLUSHTX) drivers.  WordMaster's control flow
                                ; and instruction sequence are reproduced exactly (same assembled object code);
                                ; only the label NAMES are translated -- WM.ASM's address-derived labels (Lxxxx)
                                ; are renamed descriptively, which changes nothing in the assembled bytes.
                                ; Every routine cites its WM.ASM source line, so it still diffs against WM.ASM.
                                ;
                                ; WHAT IS HERE: the load path is FILLBUF and the save path SAVCLO/FLUSHTX --
                                ; the read and write sides of WordMaster's pager.  The window slides along a
                                ; file bigger than RAM through the eviction seam: MKROOM (SPILL forward, SPILLB
                                ; backward), REWIND, PAGEBOT, PAGEDIR/PAGEWIN/PGNEED and NEEDIN.  UPDMARK keeps
                                ; the three record marks (OUTREC/SRCREC/BAKREC) that let PAGEOUT and PAGEBOT
                                ; tell "already on disk" from "must transfer", so nothing is written twice or
                                ; lost; every mark starts each file at zero, as WM's per-file work-variable
                                ; clear leaves it.
                                ;
                                ; DEVIATIONS FROM WM (each is also flagged where it is):
                                ;   1. GETKEY -> KBPOLL.  RDSEC and POLLBRK drain type-ahead through WM's
                                ;      GETKEY; the ring is KEY.MAC's, so they call its KBPOLL.  POLLBRK keeps
                                ;      only WM's non-interruptible path (no ^C 'INTERRUPTED').  Harnesses
                                ;      without KEY.MAC supply a KBPOLL RET stub.
                                ;   2. FATAL -> JMP ERRMSG.  WM's FATAL (WM 5429) prints via CRLF/PUTSTR/CONOUT
                                ;      then JMP ABORT (screen + stack-unwind, neither exists).  It shares the
                                ;      'CALL x / DB msg,0' convention with ERRMSG, so FATAL just enters ERRMSG's
                                ;      tail (print msg, set ERRFLG, warm-boot).  Only reached on a disk error.
                                ;   3. OPENFIL / SAVEFIL wrappers.  WM's file-open is inline INIT code (WM
                                ;      412-519) and its save is ENDEDIT reached from the command loop (557-567);
                                ;      neither is a CALLable unit.  These two entry points run WM's exact
                                ;      instruction sequences verbatim, with the source FCB pre-staged at 005CH
                                ;      by CP/M from the command tail.  Same-drive / user-0 only: the multi-drive
                                ;      DRVMAP / DSTDRV branches (INIT 458-493) are omitted -- the bodies kept
                                ;      are verbatim.  A write to another drive is WRTO's, below.
                                ;   4. FILLBUF stores the last record's byte count (80H) for a full record with
                                ;      no ^Z, which WM does not -- WM's end-of-file bug; see FILLBUF.
                                ;   5. DISCRD skips the work-file deletes when this session never wrote a work
                                ;      record; see DISCRD.
                                ;   6. The backup work file is VIBACKUP.$$$, where WM names it WMBACKUP.$$$
                                ;      (BAKNAM).  Same length, so no layout moves.
                                ;   7. MEMSHT calls BUF.MAC's MEMERR, not ERRMSG: running out of room ends
                                ;      the key and leaves the editor up, as WM's prompt is left up (issue
                                ;      #39; BUF.MAC's deviation 3).
                                ;   8. The unchanged front (issue #34, part A).  SAMREC counts the records at
                                ;      the front of the file that are still the source's own: FFFFH at every
                                ;      open, lowered by UPDMARK beside OUTREC.  PAGEOUT does not write such a
                                ;      record (it raises OUTREC past it instead), REWIND reads it back from the
                                ;      source through a second FCB, SRCFCB, and SAVCLO copies them into
                                ;      name.$$$ first (SVFRNT), then writes the ones the save passes from RAM
                                ;      (SAVMOD).  So moving through a file writes nothing until it is edited,
                                ;      and only from the first edit on.  See PAGEOUT, REWIND, SAVCLO.
                                ;   9. WRREC keeps the record number when it makes the work file.  WM's
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-1


                                ;      DELRST zeroes it, which is harmless while the first write is always
                                ;      record 0; with deviation 8 the first can be any record.
                                ;
                                ; APPENDED (not WM), tagged where each starts: REOPEN/SEEKTO/OPENZ (':w' keeps
                                ; editing), TFCB/WRTO/TEXIST/DISCRD/CNTLF (':w name', ':e', a buffer with no
                                ; name), PGTOPM (the count of times the pager moved TXTBEG) and TOPLF with
                                ; TLFADD/TLFSUB (the line feeds behind the window, kept in PAGEOUT and REWIND),
                                ; SCNREC (a record of the text outside the window, read where it lies) and
                                ; PGJUMP (a far move up on an unchanged file reads it again from its start).
                                ;============================================================
                                
  0000                          WBOOT	EQU	0
  0005                          BDOS	EQU	5
  001A                          EOF	EQU	1AH		; ^Z
  0008                          BS	EQU	08H
  0200                          PGINIT	EQU	200H		; WM 20 -- cold WRLIM/RDLIM (no-spill window)
                                
                                ;--- entry points the harness / editor calls -------------------------------
                                	PUBLIC	OPENFIL
                                	PUBLIC	RENAME, BAKEXT	; PSV.MAC -- the pager tests' SAVEFIL
                                	PUBLIC	FILLBUF, SAVCLO
                                ;--- the disk seam BUF.MAC reaches -----------------------------------------
                                	PUBLIC	MKROOM, REWIND, UPDMARK, MARKGB
                                	PUBLIC	SPILL		; WM 4386 -- 'u' makes its room (BUF.MAC URROOM)
                                ;--- scroll/search paging drivers (BUF.MAC's PAGESTP / SCRLST reach them)
                                	PUBLIC	PAGEDIR, PAGEWIN
                                	PUBLIC	POLLBRK		; break poll (CNTTST tail-calls it)
                                	PUBLIC	MOREIN		; WM 4743 -- GOLINE (BUF.MAC) tests it
                                ;--- data the harness reads to check state ---------------------------------
                                	PUBLIC	INRDY		; NZ while input remains (harness scroll loop)
                                ;--- on-demand page-in (BUF.MAC RGET) and the renderer's spill guard ------------
                                	PUBLIC	NEEDIN		; WM 4617 -- RGET pages input in
                                ;--- APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): vi :w keeps editing (WM 'H' on the same file) ---
                                	PUBLIC	REOPEN, SEEKTO, OPENZ
                                ;--- APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): vi :w name, :e, a buffer with no name ---------
                                	PUBLIC	WRTO, TEXIST, DISCRD, CNTLF
                                ;--- APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): a search's wrapped pass reads, it does not page
                                	PUBLIC	SCNREC
                                ;--- APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): a far move up on an unchanged file starts over
                                	PUBLIC	PGJUMP
                                	EXTRN	BINIT		; BUF.MAC -- WM L02F2 gap-pointer reset
                                	EXTRN	WRTYP, SECBUF	; RSV.MAC -- held above the image (see RSV.MAC)
                                
                                ;--- gap-buffer primitives + cells this layer drives (from BUF.MAC) ---------
                                	EXTRN	MEMCPY, CMP16, LDHLI, PRSPAN, BUFSUM
                                	EXTRN	PUTHOLE, PUTCUR, SUBHD, SUBCP2, POPRET, ERRMSG, MEMERR
                                	EXTRN	TXTBEG, GAPBEG, GAPEND, TXTEND, BUFEND
                                	EXTRN	KBPOLL		; KEY.MAC -- WM GETKEY (type-ahead drain)
                                
  0000'                         	CSEG
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; OPENFIL -- open the source file (staged at 005CH by CP/M) and read it into
                                ; the gap buffer.  Verbatim INIT subset (WM 412-518) + CMDINI limits (854);
                                ; wrapper glue only (deviation 3).  BINIT must have run first.
                                ;============================================================
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-2


  0000'                         OPENFIL:
  0000'   21 0200               	LXI	H,PGINIT	; WM 854 (CMDINI) -- no-spill window
  0003'   22 0000*              	SHLD	WRLIM
  0006'   22 0000*              	SHLD	RDLIM
  0009'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFEND		; WM 388/412 -- H = high byte of BUFEND
  000C'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  000D'   CD 02E6'              	CALL	PGCONST		; paging constants (BUFHI/BUFLO/IOBATCH/...)
  0010'   21 005C               	LXI	H,5CH		; build OUTFCB as a copy of the source FCB
  0013'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0016'   01 0010               	LXI	B,10H
  0019'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY		; WM 462-463 -- 16-byte FCB header copy
  001C'   21 09F2'              	LXI	H,BAKTYP	; set OUTFCB type = '$$$'  (WM 516-517)
  001F'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTTYP
  0022'   CD 08CD'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  0025'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB	; zero OUTFCB random-record bytes
  0028'   CD 0835'              	CALL	ZERORR
  002B'   3A 005C               	LDA	5CH		; build BAKFCB = drive + 'VIBACKUP$$$'
  002E'   32 0000*              	STA	BAKFCB		; WM 479-485
  0031'   21 09EA'              	LXI	H,BAKNAM
  0034'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,BAKFCB
  0037'   13                    	INX	D
  0038'   01 000B               	LXI	B,0BH
  003B'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY
  003E'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB	; delete any stale name.$$$  (WM 513-514)
  0041'   CD 0864'              	CALL	DELF
  0044'   21 09F5'              	LXI	H,BAKEXT	; delete any stale name.BAK  (WM 510-517):
  0047'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTTYP	;   point OUTTYP at 'BAK', delete, restore '$$$'
  004A'   CD 08CD'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  004D'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0050'   CD 0864'              	CALL	DELF
  0053'   21 09F2'              	LXI	H,BAKTYP
  0056'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTTYP
  0059'   CD 08CD'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  005C'   11 005C               	LXI	D,5CH		; open the source file  (WM 496-505)
  005F'   CD 0830'              	CALL	OPENF
  0062'   3E FF                 	MVI	A,0FFH
  0064'   CA 0085'              	JZ	OPNEW
  0067'   32 005B               	STA	5BH		; source has data (input side live)
  006A'   21 005C               	LXI	H,5CH		; DEVIATION 8: SRCFCB is the source FCB as the
  006D'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SRCFCB	;   open left it, so reading the records above
  0070'   01 0020               	LXI	B,20H		;   the window back costs no directory search.
  0073'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY		;   CP/M 2.2 keeps nothing of an open file
  0076'   21 0020*              	LXI	H,SRCFCB+20H	;   outside its FCB.  Record, and the 'written'
  0079'   06 04                 	MVI	B,4H		;   byte SETREC reads, start at zero.
  007B'   36 00                 OPSZ:	MVI	M,0H
  007D'   23                    	INX	H
  007E'   05                    	DCR	B
  007F'   C2 007B'              	JNZ	OPSZ
  0082'   C3 0088'              	JMP	OPRD
  0085'                         OPNEW:				; source not found -> new file
  0085'   32 0000*              	STA	NEWFIL
  0088'                         OPRD:				; cold-start the pager state.  WM does this by
  0088'   AF                    	XRA	A		;   zeroing its whole work-variable area (WM
  0089'   32 0000*              	STA	BAKRDY		;   369-373, the L0307 clear loop over TXTROWS..
  008C'   32 0000*              	STA	OUTACT		 ;   2730): every deque mark -- OUTACT/OUTPOS/BAKPOS/
  008F'   32 0000*              	STA	INLEN		;   INLEN/OUTREC/SRCREC/BAKREC -- lives in that
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-3


  0092'   32 0000*              	STA	DIRFLG		;   region, so its true cold value is ZERO.  With
  0095'   32 0000*              	STA	SAVMOD		; (deviation 8) not saving
  0098'   21 0000               	LXI	H,0H		;   the real UPDMARK maintaining them (below), no
  009B'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTREC		;   bias is needed: at cold OUTPOS=0 and UPDMARK
  009E'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SRCREC		;   lowers it on an edit; PAGEOUT raises it.
  00A1'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BAKREC
  00A4'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BAKPOS
  00A7'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTPOS
  00AA'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTHI		; (appended) name.$$$ holds no record yet
  00AD'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TOPLF		; (appended) no line is behind the window yet
  00B0'   2B                    	DCX	H		; DEVIATION 8: the source holds all of it
  00B1'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SAMREC
  00B4'   CD 045E'              	CALL	FILLBUF		; WM 518 -- read the file into the buffer
  00B7'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): vi ':w' saves and keeps editing.  WM has no such
                                ; command -- its 'H' (EDNEXT, WM 525-545) ends the edit and re-inits for the
                                ; next file.  REOPEN is that re-init applied to the same file, and SEEKTO
                                ; pages the saved text back in up to the cursor's old place, flushing and
                                ; refilling exactly as the save loop (SAVCLO) does.  Without this, the editor
                                ; kept running on the flushed buffer and closed/renamed FCBs after a ':w'.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;REOPEN -- after a save: re-open the file named at 005CH and load its start.
  00B8'                         REOPEN:
  00B8'   CD 0841'              	CALL	CLSBAK		; WM 526 (EDNEXT)
  00BB'   CD 0000*              	CALL	BINIT		; WM L02F2 -- reset the gap pointers
                                ;OPENZ -- OPENFIL after WM's L02F2 clears (WM 369-376): the source FCB's input
                                ; flag, extent, record count and random record, and NEWFIL.  At start-up the
                                ; input flag (005BH) holds whatever the last program left there; a file that
                                ; is not found must not be read from.
  00BE'                         OPENZ:
  00BE'   AF                    	XRA	A
  00BF'   32 005B               	STA	5BH
  00C2'   32 0068               	STA	68H
  00C5'   32 006B               	STA	6BH
  00C8'   32 007D               	STA	7DH
  00CB'   32 0000*              	STA	NEWFIL
  00CE'   C3 0000'              	JMP	OPENFIL		; WM INIT: FCBs, stale-file deletes, open, fill
                                
                                ;SEEKTO -- DE = record, A = byte (0-127) of a file position: page forward
                                ;until that position is in the window.  HL = its logical offset (the end of
                                ;the text if the file is shorter).  OUTPOS*128 is TXTBEG's file position.
  00D1'                         SEEKTO:
  00D1'   32 0000*              	STA	SKBYT
  00D4'   EB                    	XCHG
  00D5'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SKREC
  00D8'                         SKLP:
  00D8'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  00DB'   EB                    	XCHG
  00DC'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SKREC
  00DF'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; HL = records past TXTBEG's
  00E2'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  00E3'   FE 02                 	CPI	2H
  00E5'   D2 0106'              	JNC	SKMORE		; >= 200H records: not in the window
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-4


  00E8'   1F                    	RAR			; CY = bit 8 (H is 0 or 1)
  00E9'   7D                    	MOV	A,L
  00EA'   1F                    	RAR			; A = bits 8-1, CY = bit 0
  00EB'   57                    	MOV	D,A
  00EC'   3E 00                 	MVI	A,0
  00EE'   1F                    	RAR			; A = bit 0 << 7
  00EF'   5F                    	MOV	E,A
  00F0'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SKBYT
  00F3'   B3                    	ORA	E
  00F4'   5F                    	MOV	E,A		; DE = HL*128 + byte: the target offset
  00F5'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  00F6'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
  00F9'   EB                    	XCHG
  00FA'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  00FD'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  0100'   EB                    	XCHG			; DE = text in the window
  0101'   E1                    	POP	H		; HL = target
  0102'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff length < target
  0105'   D0                    	RNC			; in the window
  0106'                         SKMORE:
  0106'   CD 03DE'              	CALL	FLUSHTX		; WM 4850 (SAVCLO): write it all, refill
  0109'   CD 0444'              	CALL	FILLBF2
  010C'   D2 00D8'              	JNC	SKLP
  010F'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG		; no more input: the end of the text
  0112'   EB                    	XCHG
  0113'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  0116'   C3 0000*              	JMP	SUBHD
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): a far move up starts again from the file's start
                                ; (issue #34, part B).  WM pages back to text above the window record by
                                ; record, sliding the window down for every batch, and on a file that has not
                                ; changed since it was opened or written that text is all still the source's
                                ; (deviation 8): the window can be dropped and the source read again from
                                ; record 0, as OPENFIL reads it, and the move goes on forward from there.
                                ; Nothing is lost by it.  SAMREC is FFFFH only while no change has been made,
                                ; so the window holds no change, nothing is in name.$$$ and VIBACKUP.$$$
                                ; holds only text the source holds too.  BINIT is not called: the yank
                                ; register and the undo region, below TXTBEG, stay as they are.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;PGJUMP -- HL = how far the target lies from the file's start, DE = how far
                                ;the window's top does, both in lines or both in records.  If the target is
                                ;less than half as far down as the window's top and SAMREC is FFFFH, empty the
                                ;window (the gap takes all of it), put the source back at record 0, reset the
                                ;marks and fill the window again as OPRD does: CY, the cursor at the start of
                                ;the text.  Otherwise NC and nothing done.
  0119'                         PGJUMP:
  0119'   29                    	DAD	H		; HL = twice the target
  011A'   3F                    	CMC
  011B'   D0                    	RNC			; that overflowed: far down, no
  011C'   EB                    	XCHG
  011D'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff twice the target < the window's top
  0120'   D0                    	RNC
  0121'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC
  0124'   23                    	INX	H
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-5


  0125'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  0126'   B5                    	ORA	L		; (and NC)
  0127'   C0                    	RNZ			; changed since it was opened or written
  0128'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
  012B'   22 0000*              	SHLD	GAPBEG
  012E'   22 0000*              	SHLD	GAPEND
  0131'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TXTEND
  0134'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	PGTOPM		; the window's top moved: 'u' and the screen
  0137'   23                    	INX	H		;   read this
  0138'   22 0000*              	SHLD	PGTOPM
  013B'   21 0000               	LXI	H,0H
  013E'   22 007E               	SHLD	7EH		; the source's next record is record 0 (SETREC
  0141'   3D                    	DCR	A		;   opens extent 0 for it), and it has data
  0142'   32 005B               	STA	5BH
  0145'   CD 0088'              	CALL	OPRD		; every mark to zero, then FILLBUF
  0148'   37                    	STC
  0149'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): the text outside the window, read where it lies.
                                ; vi's search wraps round the file, and WM's find can only page the window
                                ; there and back again to look (CMD.MAC SCAN, issue #35).  This reads one
                                ; record of it into SECBUF with WM's own RDSEC and CLNSEC, through the FCB the
                                ; pager would have read it through, and puts that FCB's record word and its
                                ; has-data flag back after -- so the pager never knows.  Only the open extent
                                ; moves, and SETREC re-opens the right one on the pager's next transfer, as it
                                ; does after a REWIND.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;SCNREC -- HL = a record, A = which: 0 one above the window (0 to OUTPOS-1:
                                ;below SAMREC it is the source's own, and from there name.$$$'s, as RWNREC
                                ;has it), 1 one of VIBACKUP.$$$'s, 2 one of the source's below the window.
                                ;Cleaned as FILLBUF cleans what it reads; name.$$$'s is read raw, as REWIND
                                ;reads it.  A = the bytes of text in it.  CY = its stream ended in it (a ^Z)
                                ;or before it (there is no such record: A = 0).
  014A'                         SCNREC:
  014A'   EB                    	XCHG			; DE = the record
  014B'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BAKFCB
  014E'   3D                    	DCR	A
  014F'   CA 016C'              	JZ	SCNCLN		; 1: the backup stack
  0152'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SRCFCB
  0155'   F2 016C'              	JP	SCNCLN		; 2: the source below
  0158'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC		; 0: above
  015B'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff the record < SAMREC
  015E'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SRCFCB
  0161'   DA 016C'              	JC	SCNCLN
  0164'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,OUTFCB
  0167'   06 00                 	MVI	B,0		; name.$$$'s: raw
  0169'   C3 016E'              	JMP	SCNGO
  016C'                         SCNCLN:
  016C'   06 01                 	MVI	B,1
  016E'                         SCNGO:				; HL = the FCB, DE = the record, B = 1 to clean
  016E'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  016F'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0170'   2B                    	DCX	H
  0171'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-6


  0172'   32 0000*              	STA	SCNFLG		; its has-data flag: an EOF or a ^Z clears it
  0175'   01 0023               	LXI	B,23H
  0178'   09                    	DAD	B		; FCB+22H, its record word
  0179'   4E                    	MOV	C,M
  017A'   73                    	MOV	M,E
  017B'   23                    	INX	H
  017C'   46                    	MOV	B,M
  017D'   72                    	MOV	M,D
  017E'   60                    	MOV	H,B
  017F'   69                    	MOV	L,C
  0180'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCNOLD		; the record word as the pager left it
  0183'   D1                    	POP	D		; DE = the FCB
  0184'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SECBUF
  0187'   CD 08DE'              	CALL	RDSEC		; CY: there is no such record (A = 0)
  018A'   C1                    	POP	B
  018B'   DA 019B'              	JC	SCNEND
  018E'   3E 80                 	MVI	A,80H
  0190'   05                    	DCR	B
  0191'   C2 019B'              	JNZ	SCNEND		; raw: all of it, NC
  0194'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SECBUF
  0197'   CD 04A4'              	CALL	CLNSEC		; CY: all of it; NC: a ^Z, A = the bytes before
  019A'   3F                    	CMC
  019B'                         SCNEND:
  019B'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  019C'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SCNFLG
  019F'   EB                    	XCHG			; HL = the FCB
  01A0'   2B                    	DCX	H
  01A1'   77                    	MOV	M,A
  01A2'   11 0023               	LXI	D,23H
  01A5'   19                    	DAD	D
  01A6'   EB                    	XCHG
  01A7'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCNOLD
  01AA'   EB                    	XCHG
  01AB'   73                    	MOV	M,E
  01AC'   23                    	INX	H
  01AD'   72                    	MOV	M,D
  01AE'   F1                    	POP	PSW
  01AF'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): vi writes the text to a name of its own (:w name,
                                ; and a buffer that has no name) and drops it for another file (:e).  WM always
                                ; writes back to the file it read.  These use WM's own primitives: SAVCLO for
                                ; the flush, RENAME for the backup, RENF, DELF, MAKEF, OPENF, CLOSEF.
                                ; TFCB holds the target name; the vi layer fills its drive, name and type
                                ; (bytes 0-11) and zeroes the rest.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;TEXIST -- Z iff no file has TFCB's name.
  01B0'                         TEXIST:
  01B0'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  01B3'   CD 0816'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  01B6'   11                    	DB	11H		; search for the first match
  01B7'   3C                    	INR	A
  01B8'   C9                    	RET
                                
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-7


                                ;WRTO -- write the whole text to the file named in TFCB (the edit is flushed
                                ; to name.$$$, as WM's ENDEDIT does).  A <> 0: a file already there becomes
                                ; name.BAK (WM ENDEDIT); A = 0: it is deleted (vim overwrites it).  Then
                                ; name.$$$ takes TFCB's name, by RENF on its own drive or by a copy to another
                                ; drive.  REOPEN must follow (from TFCB's name).
  01B9'                         WRTO:
  01B9'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  01BA'   CD 0535'              	CALL	SAVCLO		; WM 558 (ENDEDIT)
  01BD'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  01C0'   F1                    	POP	PSW
  01C1'   B7                    	ORA	A
  01C2'   CA 01EF'              	JZ	WRDEL
  01C5'   21 0009*              	LXI	H,TFCB+9	; delete any old name.BAK
  01C8'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,WRTYP
  01CB'   CD 08CD'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  01CE'   11 0009*              	LXI	D,TFCB+9
  01D1'   CD 08CA'              	CALL	CPYBAK
  01D4'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  01D7'   CD 0864'              	CALL	DELF
  01DA'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,WRTYP
  01DD'   11 0009*              	LXI	D,TFCB+9
  01E0'   CD 08CD'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  01E3'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB		; name -> name.BAK (WM 562)
  01E6'   21 09F5'              	LXI	H,BAKEXT
  01E9'   CD 088E'              	CALL	RENAME
  01EC'   C3 01F2'              	JMP	WRMOV
  01EF'                         WRDEL:
  01EF'   CD 0864'              	CALL	DELF
  01F2'                         WRMOV:
  01F2'   3A 0000*              	LDA	OUTFCB
  01F5'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TFCB
  01F8'   BE                    	CMP	M
  01F9'   C2 021E'              	JNZ	WRCPY		; another drive
  01FC'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,OUTFCB	; RENF block: name.$$$, then TFCB's name
  01FF'   11 0010*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB+10H
  0202'   01 0010               	LXI	B,10H
  0205'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY
  0208'   21 0001*              	LXI	H,TFCB+1
  020B'   11 0011*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB+11H
  020E'   01 000B               	LXI	B,0BH
  0211'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY
  0214'   AF                    	XRA	A
  0215'   32 0010*              	STA	OUTFCB+10H	; the new name's drive byte is 0 (as RENAME)
  0218'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  021B'   C3 08AD'              	JMP	RENF		; WM 566
  021E'                         WRCPY:				; name.$$$ copied record by record
  021E'   AF                    	XRA	A		; extent 0, record 0 on both
  021F'   32 000C*              	STA	OUTFCB+0CH
  0222'   32 0020*              	STA	OUTFCB+20H
  0225'   32 0020*              	STA	TFCB+20H
  0228'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  022B'   CD 0830'              	CALL	OPENF
  022E'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  0231'   CD 0870'              	CALL	DELRST		; make the new file
  0234'                         WRCLP:
  0234'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-8


  0237'   CD 0816'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  023A'   14                    	DB	14H		; read the next record
  023B'   B7                    	ORA	A
  023C'   C2 024D'              	JNZ	WRCEND
  023F'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  0242'   CD 0816'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  0245'   15                    	DB	15H		; write it
  0246'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0247'   CA 0234'              	JZ	WRCLP
  024A'   C3 092C'              	JMP	DSKERR
  024D'                         WRCEND:
  024D'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  0250'   CD 084B'              	CALL	CLOSEF
  0253'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0256'   C3 0864'              	JMP	DELF
                                
                                ;DISCRD -- drop the edit: delete name.$$$ and VIBACKUP$$$ (WM EDEND, 581).
                                ;DEVIATION (not WordMaster): both are skipped when this session never wrote a
                                ;work record at all (WRKMAD clear), because then neither file can exist.  A BDOS
                                ;delete scans the whole directory whether or not the name is on it -- the best
                                ;part of a second each on a large drive -- and ':q' on a text that never spilled
                                ;paid it twice for nothing.  The per-file [FCB-2]/[FCB-1] flags will NOT do:
                                ;reading the backup back to its end clears them while the file is still there,
                                ;which is why WM's EDEND deletes unconditionally.
  0259'                         DISCRD:
  0259'   3A 0000*              	LDA	WRKMAD
  025C'   B7                    	ORA	A
  025D'   C8                    	RZ			; no work file was ever made: nothing to drop
  025E'   AF                    	XRA	A
  025F'   32 0000*              	STA	WRKMAD		; the deletes below leave nothing to drop again
  0262'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0265'   CD 0864'              	CALL	DELF
  0268'   C3 085E'              	JMP	KILLBAK
                                
                                ;CNTLF -- HL = the line feeds before the cursor: TOPLF for the records behind
                                ;the window, plus a scan of the text from TXTBEG to the gap.  It reads no disk.
  026B'                         CNTLF:
  026B'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TOPLF
  026E'   22 0000*              	SHLD	CLCNT
  0271'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
  0274'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0275'   EB                    	XCHG
  0276'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPBEG
  0279'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  027C'   EB                    	XCHG			; DE = the text before the gap
  027D'   E1                    	POP	H
  027E'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  027F'   CD 02BF'              	CALL	CLBYTS
  0282'   C1                    	POP	B
  0283'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	CLCNT
  0286'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;TLFADD / TLFSUB -- the sector at HL leaves the window's top (PAGEOUT) or comes
                                ;back to it (REWIND): TOPLF gains or loses its line feeds.  TOPLF is then the
                                ;line feeds in output records 0 to OUTPOS-1 at all times, which is what CNTLF
                                ;used to read those records back to find.  Keeps every register and the flags.
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-9


  0287'                         TLFADD:
  0287'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  0288'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0289'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  028A'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  028B'   CD 02AA'              	CALL	TLFSEC
  028E'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TOPLF
  0291'   19                    	DAD	D
  0292'   C3 02A2'              	JMP	TLFSTO
  0295'                         TLFSUB:
  0295'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  0296'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0297'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0298'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0299'   CD 02AA'              	CALL	TLFSEC
  029C'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TOPLF
  029F'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  02A2'                         TLFSTO:
  02A2'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TOPLF
  02A5'   E1                    	POP	H
  02A6'   D1                    	POP	D
  02A7'   C1                    	POP	B
  02A8'   F1                    	POP	PSW
  02A9'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;TLFSEC -- DE = the line feeds in the 128 bytes at HL.  A window of records
                                ;the source still holds leaves with no disk call (DEVIATION 8), so this is
                                ;where a long slide takes a key typed meanwhile (#40).
  02AA'                         TLFSEC:
  02AA'   CD 0000*              	CALL	KBPOLL
  02AD'   11 0000               	LXI	D,0
  02B0'   06 80                 	MVI	B,80H
  02B2'                         TLFLP:
  02B2'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  02B3'   23                    	INX	H
  02B4'   FE 0A                 	CPI	0AH
  02B6'   C2 02BA'              	JNZ	TLFNX
  02B9'   13                    	INX	D
  02BA'                         TLFNX:
  02BA'   05                    	DCR	B
  02BB'   C2 02B2'              	JNZ	TLFLP
  02BE'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;CLBYTS -- HL = text, DE = its length: CLCNT += its line feeds.  A whole
                                ;window is some 23 K, half a second: KBPOLL every 256 bytes takes a key
                                ;typed meanwhile (#40), as the copy loops do.  Clobbers BC.
  02BF'                         CLBYTS:
  02BF'   42                    	MOV	B,D
  02C0'   4B                    	MOV	C,E		; BC = the length
  02C1'   EB                    	XCHG
  02C2'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	CLCNT
  02C5'   EB                    	XCHG			; DE = the count, HL = the text
  02C6'   04                    	INR	B
  02C7'   0C                    	INR	C
  02C8'   C3 02D3'              	JMP	CLBCT
  02CB'   7E                    CLBLP:	MOV	A,M
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-10


  02CC'   23                    	INX	H
  02CD'   FE 0A                 	CPI	0AH
  02CF'   C2 02D3'              	JNZ	CLBCT
  02D2'   13                    	INX	D
  02D3'   0D                    CLBCT:	DCR	C
  02D4'   C2 02CB'              	JNZ	CLBLP
  02D7'   05                    	DCR	B
  02D8'   CA 02E1'              	JZ	CLBEND
  02DB'   CD 0000*              	CALL	KBPOLL		; 256 bytes counted
  02DE'   C3 02CB'              	JMP	CLBLP
  02E1'   EB                    CLBEND:	XCHG
  02E2'   22 0000*              	SHLD	CLCNT
  02E5'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; PAGING CONSTANTS -- WM 412-447.  From A/H = high byte of BUFEND, derive the
                                ; batch/margin sizing and the free-space water marks the load/spill path reads.
                                ;============================================================
  02E6'                         PGCONST:			; WM 412
  02E6'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  02E7'   B7                    	ORA	A
  02E8'   1F                    	RAR
  02E9'   1F                    	RAR
  02EA'   1F                    	RAR
  02EB'   3C                    	INR	A
  02EC'   3C                    	INR	A
  02ED'   E6 3C                 	ANI	3CH
  02EF'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  02F0'   32 0000*              	STA	PGSCAL
  02F3'   07                    	RLC
  02F4'   32 0000*              	STA	PGSCL2
  02F7'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  02F8'   FE 08                 	CPI	BS
  02FA'   D2 02FF'              	JNC	PGCON1
  02FD'   3E 08                 	MVI	A,BS
  02FF'                         PGCON1:				 ; WM 430
  02FF'   32 0000*              	STA	PGMARGN
  0302'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  0303'   FE 64                 	CPI	64H
  0305'   21 0400               	LXI	H,400H
  0308'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BUFLO
  030B'   DA 030F'              	JC	PGCON2
  030E'   29                    	DAD	H
  030F'                         PGCON2:				 ; WM 439
  030F'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BUFHI
  0312'   3E 08                 	MVI	A,BS
  0314'   32 0000*              	STA	PGSCRA
  0317'   DA 031B'              	JC	PGCON3
  031A'   87                    	ADD	A
  031B'                         PGCON3:				 ; WM 446
  031B'   32 0000*              	STA	IOBATCH
  031E'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; SPILL / PAGEOUT / FLUSHTX -- the output (write-behind) side.  RAM-only, SPILL
                                ; no-ops (CKWRLIM) on load and FLUSHTX drains the whole buffer on save.
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-11


                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;SPILL -- WM 4386: write-behind a batch of TXTBEG-side sectors to OUTFCB.
  031F'                         SPILL:				; WM 4386
  031F'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0320'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0321'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0322'   CD 034E'              	CALL	PAGEOUT
  0325'   DA 0000*              	JC	POPRET
  0328'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SPLCNT
  032B'   34                    	INR	M
  032C'   46                    	MOV	B,M
  032D'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,PGSCL2
  0330'   AF                    	XRA	A
  0331'                         SPLSUM:				 ; WM 4398
  0331'   86                    	ADD	M
  0332'   05                    	DCR	B
  0333'   C2 0331'              	JNZ	SPLSUM
  0336'   3D                    	DCR	A
  0337'   F6 07                 	ORI	7H
  0339'   4F                    	MOV	C,A
  033A'   3A 0000*              	LDA	IOBATCH
  033D'   3D                    	DCR	A
  033E'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  033F'                         SPLLP:				; WM 4409
  033F'   CD 034E'              	CALL	PAGEOUT
  0342'   05                    	DCR	B
  0343'   CA 034A'              	JZ	SPLDON
  0346'   0D                    	DCR	C
  0347'   C2 033F'              	JNZ	SPLLP
  034A'                         SPLDON:				 ; WM 4416
  034A'   B7                    	ORA	A
  034B'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;PAGEOUT -- WM 4439: spill one sector at TXTBEG to OUTFCB, bump TXTBEG.
                                ;DEVIATION 8: a record below SAMREC is the source's own and is not written;
                                ;OUTREC rises past it, so OUTREC still equals OUTPOS at every fresh write
                                ;(POFRSH adds one to OUTREC, not to OUTPOS).  OUTREC then means "valid in
                                ;name.$$$ or in the source".  While SAVCLO saves (SAVMOD), such a record IS
                                ;written, from RAM, and OUTREC is left alone.
  034E'                         PAGEOUT:			; WM 4439
  034E'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
  0351'   CD 0628'              	CALL	CKWRLIM
  0354'   D8                    	RC
  0355'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0356'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  0359'   EB                    	XCHG
  035A'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC		; DEVIATION 8
  035D'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff OUTPOS < SAMREC
  0360'   DA 03A9'              	JC	POSAME
  0363'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTREC
  0366'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  0369'   E1                    	POP	H
  036A'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  036D'   D2 0376'              	JNC	POFRSH
  0370'   CD 0965'              	CALL	RECINC
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-12


  0373'   C3 0395'              	JMP	POADV
  0376'                         POFRSH:				 ; WM 4454 -- write a fresh output record
  0376'   CD 095F'              	CALL	WRRECP
  0379'   EB                    	XCHG
  037A'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTREC
  037D'   23                    	INX	H
  037E'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTREC
  0381'   D5                    POWHI:	PUSH	D		; (appended) OUTHI follows the most records
  0382'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTHI		;   name.$$$ has ever held; OUTREC cannot
  0385'   EB                    	XCHG			;   say, an edit behind it brings it down
  0386'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  0389'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  038C'   D2 0392'              	JNC	POHI
  038F'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTHI
  0392'   D1                    POHI:	POP	D
  0393'   EB                    	XCHG
  0394'   04                    	INR	B
  0395'                         POADV:				; WM 4463 -- advance TXTBEG past the sector
  0395'   CD 0287'              	CALL	TLFADD		; (appended) its line feeds are behind the
                                				;   window now
  0398'   11 0080               	LXI	D,80H
  039B'   19                    	DAD	D
  039C'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TXTBEG
  039F'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  03A0'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	PGTOPM		; (appended) the window's top moved: 'u' reads
  03A3'   23                    	INX	H		;   this to know its offsets have shifted
  03A4'   22 0000*              	SHLD	PGTOPM
  03A7'   E1                    	POP	H
  03A8'   C9                    	RET
  03A9'                         POSAME:				; DEVIATION 8: the source holds this record
  03A9'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SAVMOD
  03AC'   B7                    	ORA	A
  03AD'   C2 03D3'              	JNZ	POSAVE
  03B0'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTREC
  03B3'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff OUTPOS < OUTREC: counted already, as
  03B6'   DA 03C9'              	JC	POSAM1		;   WM skips a record already written
  03B9'   13                    	INX	D
  03BA'   EB                    	XCHG
  03BB'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTREC		; OUTREC = OUTPOS+1
  03BE'   E1                    	POP	H
  03BF'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  03C2'   CD 0965'              	CALL	RECINC		; past it, unwritten -- and where WM would have
  03C5'   04                    	INR	B		;   written it, SPILL's batch counts it as WM's
  03C6'   C3 0395'              	JMP	POADV		;   does, so a first pass empties the window
  03C9'   E1                    POSAM1:	POP	H
  03CA'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  03CD'   CD 0965'              	CALL	RECINC
  03D0'   C3 0395'              	JMP	POADV
  03D3'   E1                    POSAVE:	POP	H		; saving: write it from RAM
  03D4'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  03D7'   CD 095F'              	CALL	WRRECP
  03DA'   EB                    	XCHG
  03DB'   C3 0381'              	JMP	POWHI
                                
                                ;FLUSHTX -- WM 4471: collapse the gap and PAGEOUT every remaining sector.
  03DE'                         FLUSHTX:			; WM 4471
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-13


  03DE'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  03DF'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  03E0'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  03E1'   21 0081               	LXI	H,81H
  03E4'   22 0000*              	SHLD	WRLIM
  03E7'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND
  03EA'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PUTHOLE
  03ED'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  03F0'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PUTCUR
  03F3'                         FLXLP:				; WM 4482 -- flush loop
  03F3'   CD 034E'              	CALL	PAGEOUT
  03F6'   D2 03F3'              	JNC	FLXLP
  03F9'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;STAGSEC -- WM 4588: stage a short final record into SECBUF, ^Z-pad the tail.
  03FC'                         STAGSEC:			; WM 4588
  03FC'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  03FD'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  03FE'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SECBUF
  0401'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0402'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  0403'   0E 82                 	MVI	C,82H
  0405'   04                    	INR	B
  0406'   2B                    	DCX	H
  0407'   1B                    	DCX	D
  0408'                         STGCPY:				 ; WM 4599 -- copy the partial sector
  0408'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  0409'   12                    	STAX	D
  040A'   23                    	INX	H
  040B'   13                    	INX	D
  040C'   0D                    	DCR	C
  040D'   05                    	DCR	B
  040E'   C2 0408'              	JNZ	STGCPY
  0411'                         STGPAD:				 ; WM 4608 -- pad the rest with ^Z
  0411'   3E 1A                 	MVI	A,EOF
  0413'   12                    	STAX	D
  0414'   13                    	INX	D
  0415'   0D                    	DCR	C
  0416'   C2 0411'              	JNZ	STGPAD
  0419'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; FILLBUF / RDIN / CLNSEC -- the input (read) side.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;NEEDIN -- WM 4617: page input in when the forward read (RGET) runs dry.
                                ;SPILL first if free space is under a record, then reserve and fill.
  041C'                         NEEDIN:				; WM 4617
  041C'   CD 04BF'              	CALL	INRDY
  041F'   C8                    	RZ
  0420'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0421'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0422'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0423'   CD 0000*              	CALL	BUFSUM
  0426'   21 0080               	LXI	H,80H
  0429'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-14


  042C'   EB                    	XCHG
  042D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFHI
  0430'   D2 043A'              	JNC	NDIRSV
  0433'   CD 031F'              	CALL	SPILL
  0436'   DA 04FD'              	JC	MEMSHT
  0439'   EB                    	XCHG
  043A'                         NDIRSV:				 ; WM 4633 -- reserve free space, then fill
  043A'   EB                    	XCHG
  043B'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND
  043E'   CD 04F0'              	CALL	FREEREC
  0441'   C3 046D'              	JMP	FILLRD
                                
                                ;FILLBF2 -- WM 4640: fill from input, capped at 7800H.
  0444'                         FILLBF2:			; WM 4640
  0444'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0445'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0446'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0447'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND
  044A'   11 7800               	LXI	D,7800H
  044D'   CD 0521'              	CALL	BUFFREE
  0450'   CD 04BF'              	CALL	INRDY
  0453'   CA 0488'              	JZ	FILRET
  0456'   79                    	MOV	A,C
  0457'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0458'   C2 046D'              	JNZ	FILLRD
  045B'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;FILLBUF -- WM 4659: top the window up from the input file(s).
  045E'                         FILLBUF:			; WM 4659
  045E'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  045F'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0460'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0461'   CD 04BF'              	CALL	INRDY
  0464'   CA 0488'              	JZ	FILRET
  0467'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND
  046A'   CD 04D6'              	CALL	RESVBF0
  046D'                         FILLRD:				 ; WM 4668
  046D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  0470'                         FILRLP:				 ; WM 4671 -- read & clean one input record
  0470'   CD 048B'              	CALL	RDIN
  0473'   D4 04A4'              	CNC	CLNSEC
  0476'   D2 047D'              	JNC	FILRSV		; DEVIATION (WM bug): WM is JC L1C6B, which
  0479'   B7                    	ORA	A		;   skips the store for a full record (CY,
  047A'   CA 0480'              	JZ	FILRST		;   A=80H), so a file ending on a record
  047D'   32 0000*              FILRSV: STA	INLEN		;   boundary w/o ^Z leaves INLEN=0 and PAGEBOT
                                				;   RECDECs one record too far (record saved
                                				;   twice).  Skip only RDIN's no-record case
                                				;   (CY, A=0).
  0480'                         FILRST:				 ; WM 4677
  0480'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TXTEND
  0483'   0D                    	DCR	C
  0484'   C2 0470'              	JNZ	FILRLP
  0487'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0488'                         FILRET:				 ; WM 4683
  0488'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-15


                                ;RDIN -- WM 4689: read the next input record into [HL] (backup then source).
  048B'                         RDIN:				; WM 4689
  048B'   CD 09E4'              	CALL	POLLBRK
  048E'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,BAKRDY
  0491'   1A                    	LDAX	D
  0492'   13                    	INX	D
  0493'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0494'   37                    	STC
  0495'   C4 08DA'              	CNZ	RDPREV
  0498'   D0                    	RNC
  0499'   11 005B               	LXI	D,5BH
  049C'   1A                    	LDAX	D
  049D'   13                    	INX	D
  049E'   B7                    	ORA	A
  049F'   37                    	STC
  04A0'   C4 08D3'              	CNZ	RDNEXT
  04A3'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;CLNSEC -- WM 4709: mask bit 7, stop at ^Z; return live byte count in A.
  04A4'                         CLNSEC:				; WM 4709
  04A4'   06 80                 	MVI	B,80H
  04A6'                         CLNLP:				; WM 4712
  04A6'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  04A7'   E6 7F                 	ANI	7FH
  04A9'   77                    	MOV	M,A
  04AA'   FE 1A                 	CPI	EOF
  04AC'   CA 04B8'              	JZ	CLNEOF
  04AF'   23                    	INX	H
  04B0'   05                    	DCR	B
  04B1'   C2 04A6'              	JNZ	CLNLP
  04B4'   37                    	STC
  04B5'   3E 80                 	MVI	A,80H
  04B7'   C9                    	RET
  04B8'                         CLNEOF:				 ; WM 4725 -- input EOF: return the byte count
  04B8'   CD 08EF'              	CALL	IOEOF
  04BB'   3E 80                 	MVI	A,80H
  04BD'   90                    	SUB	B
  04BE'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;INRDY -- WM 4733: NZ while any input data is still unread.
  04BF'                         INRDY:				; WM 4733
  04BF'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  04C0'   3A 005B               	LDA	5BH
  04C3'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BAKRDY
  04C6'   B6                    	ORA	M
  04C7'   37                    	STC
  04C8'   E1                    	POP	H
  04C9'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;MOREIN -- WM 4743: NZ if more input remains in the current direction
                                ;(WM's L26AA is OUTACT, the byte before OUTFCB).
  04CA'                         MOREIN:				; WM 4743
  04CA'   3A 0000*              	LDA	DIRFLG
  04CD'   B7                    	ORA	A
  04CE'   3A 0000*              	LDA	OUTACT
  04D1'   F4 04BF'              	CP	INRDY
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-16


  04D4'   B7                    	ORA	A
  04D5'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; FREE-SPACE ACCOUNTING -- WM 4786-4841.  Reserve/compute the read-ahead room.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;RESVBF0/RESVBUF -- WM 4786/4790: reserve free buffer space up to BUFHI.
  04D6'                         RESVBF0:			; WM 4786
  04D6'   11 031F'              	LXI	D,SPILL
  04D9'                         RESVBUF:			; WM 4790
  04D9'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  04DA'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFHI
  04DD'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  04DE'   CD 0000*              	CALL	BUFSUM
  04E1'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  04E4'   E1                    	POP	H
  04E5'   DC 0520'              	CC	DISPKEY
  04E8'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFLO
  04EB'   29                    	DAD	H
  04EC'   24                    	INR	H
  04ED'   24                    	INR	H
  04EE'   EB                    	XCHG
  04EF'   E1                    	POP	H
  04F0'                         FREEREC:			; WM 4806 -- free bytes -> capped record count
  04F0'   CD 0521'              	CALL	BUFFREE
  04F3'   FE 08                 	CPI	BS
  04F5'   DA 04FB'              	JC	FRECOK
  04F8'   D6 04                 	SUI	4H
  04FA'   4F                    	MOV	C,A
  04FB'                         FRECOK:				 ; WM 4813
  04FB'   B7                    	ORA	A
  04FC'   C0                    	RNZ
  04FD'                         MEMSHT:				 ; WM 4817
  04FD'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMERR		; DEVIATION 7: out of room ends the key, not
                                				;   the editor (BUF.MAC's deviation 3)
  0500'   4D 45 4D 20           	DB	'MEM SHORTAGE, TRY CLEARING QBUF',0H
  0504'   53 48 4F 52           
  0508'   54 41 47 45           
  050C'   2C 20 54 52           
  0510'   59 20 43 4C           
  0514'   45 41 52 49           
  0518'   4E 47 20 51           
  051C'   42 55 46 00           
                                
                                ;DISPKEY -- WM 2846: PCHL trampoline (call the reserve routine held in HL).
  0520'                         DISPKEY:			; WM 2846
  0520'   E9                    	PCHL
                                
                                ;BUFFREE -- WM 4827: collapse the gap and report free bytes (A/C = pages).
  0521'                         BUFFREE:			; WM 4827
  0521'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PUTHOLE
  0524'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0525'   CD 0000*              	CALL	BUFSUM
  0528'   E1                    	POP	H
  0529'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBCP2
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-17


  052C'   EB                    	XCHG
  052D'   29                    	DAD	H
  052E'                         BFRLP:				; WM 4836
  052E'   DA 052E'              	JC	BFRLP
  0531'   EB                    	XCHG
  0532'   7A                    	MOV	A,D
  0533'   4A                    	MOV	C,D
  0534'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; SAVCLO -- WM 4846: flush all buffered text to OUTFCB and close it.
                                ;============================================================
  0535'                         SAVCLO:				; WM 4846
  0535'   CD 0578'              	CALL	SVBEG		; DEVIATION 8: the source's front, counted
  0538'   CD 0444'              	CALL	FILLBF2
  053B'                         SAVLP:				; WM 4849 -- flush all, refill, repeat
  053B'   CD 03DE'              	CALL	FLUSHTX
  053E'   CD 0595'              	CALL	SVFRNT		; DEVIATION 8: ... and copied, the first time
  0541'   CD 0444'              	CALL	FILLBF2
  0544'   D2 053B'              	JNC	SAVLP
  0547'   AF                    	XRA	A		; DEVIATION 8: the pass is over
  0548'   32 0000*              	STA	SAVMOD
  054B'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TXTBEG
  054E'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PRSPAN
  0551'   CD 0000*              	CALL	LDHLI
  0554'   79                    	MOV	A,C
  0555'   CD 03FC'              	CALL	STAGSEC
  0558'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  055B'   CD 095F'              	CALL	WRRECP
  055E'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS		; DEVIATION (not WM): WM closes here.  Text
  0561'   EB                    	XCHG			;   that was paged out, rewound and then cut
  0562'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTHI		;   short leaves the old records after the
  0565'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		;   last one, and CP/M cannot drop them.  A
  0568'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB	;   part-filled last record hides them behind
  056B'   D2 084B'              	JNC	CLOSEF		;   its ^Z padding; a full one has none, and
  056E'   AF                    	XRA	A		;   the old text was read back as the file's
  056F'   CD 03FC'              	CALL	STAGSEC		;   end.  So a record of ^Z goes over the
  0572'   CD 095F'              	CALL	WRRECP		;   first of them.  It is there already:
  0575'   C3 084B'              	JMP	CLOSEF		;   this write cannot fill the disk.
                                
                                ;SVBEG / SVFRNT -- DEVIATION 8: the records above the window that the source
                                ;still holds (0 to the lower of SAMREC and OUTPOS) are not in name.$$$.  SVBEG
                                ;counts them as the save begins (SVFCNT) and sets SAVMOD, so the save writes
                                ;the other records below SAMREC from RAM as it passes them; the records from
                                ;SAMREC to OUTPOS are in name.$$$ already.  SVFRNT, after the save's first
                                ;FLUSHTX has emptied the window, copies them from the source, bit 7 cleared
                                ;as a load clears it, through the free RAM above TXTEND: as many as it holds
                                ;are read, then written.  One record at a time, read and write alternate,
                                ;and the BIOS's deblocking makes each call about ten times dearer (0.37 s a
                                ;read, measured on the simulator's 8 MB drive).  The free RAM is at least the
                                ;0D80H a full register leaves.  OUTPOS, the save's place, is put back.
  0578'                         SVBEG:
  0578'   3E FF                 	MVI	A,0FFH
  057A'   32 0000*              	STA	SAVMOD
  057D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  0580'   EB                    	XCHG
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-18


  0581'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC
  0584'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff OUTPOS < SAMREC
  0587'   D2 058B'              	JNC	SVBN
  058A'   EB                    	XCHG
  058B'   22 0000*              SVBN:	SHLD	SVFCNT
  058E'   21 0000               	LXI	H,0H
  0591'   22 0022*              	SHLD	SRCFCB+22H
  0594'   C9                    	RET
  0595'                         SVFRNT:
  0595'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SVFCNT
  0598'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  0599'   B5                    	ORA	L
  059A'   C8                    	RZ
  059B'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  059E'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  059F'   2A 0022*              	LHLD	SRCFCB+22H	; the next record: OUTPOS keeps pace with it
  05A2'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTPOS
  05A5'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND	; all the free RAM above the text (FILLBF2's
  05A8'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PUTHOLE		;   BUFFREE does the same next)
  05AB'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  05AE'   EB                    	XCHG
  05AF'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFEND
  05B2'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; HL = the free bytes above the text
  05B5'   29                    	DAD	H
  05B6'   4C                    	MOV	C,H
  05B7'   06 00                 	MVI	B,0H		; BC = the records they hold
  05B9'   79                    	MOV	A,C
  05BA'   B7                    	ORA	A
  05BB'   C2 05CE'              	JNZ	SVFFIT
  05BE'   CD 082D'              	CALL	FATAL		; cannot happen (see above): stop, never loop
  05C1'   4D 45 4D 20           	DB	'MEM SHORTAGE',0H
  05C5'   53 48 4F 52           
  05C9'   54 41 47 45           
  05CD'   00                    
  05CE'   2A 0000*              SVFFIT:	LHLD	SVFCNT
  05D1'   50                    	MOV	D,B
  05D2'   59                    	MOV	E,C
  05D3'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff they hold fewer than are left
  05D6'   DA 05DB'              	JC	SVFN
  05D9'   44                    	MOV	B,H
  05DA'   4D                    	MOV	C,L		; BC = this batch
  05DB'   50                    SVFN:	MOV	D,B
  05DC'   59                    	MOV	E,C
  05DD'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; HL = what is left after it
  05E0'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SVFCNT
  05E3'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  05E4'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  05E7'   11 0000*              SVFRD:	LXI	D,SRCFCB
  05EA'   CD 08D3'              	CALL	RDNEXT
  05ED'   D2 05FC'              	JNC	SVFOK
  05F0'   CD 082D'              	CALL	FATAL		; the source ends early: never save half of it
  05F3'   52 45 41 44           	DB	'READ ERR',0H
  05F7'   20 45 52 52           
  05FB'   00                    
  05FC'   C5                    SVFOK:	PUSH	B
  05FD'   E5                    	PUSH	H
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-19


  05FE'   CD 04A4'              	CALL	CLNSEC
  0601'   E1                    	POP	H
  0602'   C1                    	POP	B
  0603'   11 0080               	LXI	D,80H
  0606'   19                    	DAD	D
  0607'   0B                    	DCX	B
  0608'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  0609'   B1                    	ORA	C
  060A'   C2 05E7'              	JNZ	SVFRD
  060D'   C1                    	POP	B
  060E'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  0611'   11 0000*              SVFWR:	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0614'   CD 095F'              	CALL	WRRECP
  0617'   11 0080               	LXI	D,80H
  061A'   19                    	DAD	D
  061B'   0B                    	DCX	B
  061C'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  061D'   B1                    	ORA	C
  061E'   C2 0611'              	JNZ	SVFWR
  0621'   E1                    	POP	H
  0622'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTPOS
  0625'   C3 0595'              	JMP	SVFRNT		; the next batch, if any
                                
                                ;CKWRLIM -- WM 4863: CY if GAPBEG is below the PAGEOUT write limit.
  0628'                         CKWRLIM:			; WM 4863
  0628'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0629'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	WRLIM
  062C'   EB                    	XCHG
  062D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPBEG
  0630'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  0633'   EB                    	XCHG
  0634'   E1                    	POP	H
  0635'   C3 0000*              	JMP	CMP16
                                
                                ;CKRDLIM -- WM 4874: compare GAPEND against the read limit (PAGEBOT guard).
  0638'                         CKRDLIM:			; WM 4874
  0638'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0639'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	RDLIM
  063C'   EB                    	XCHG
  063D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPEND
  0640'   19                    	DAD	D
  0641'   D1                    	POP	D
  0642'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  0645'   EB                    	XCHG
  0646'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; EVICTION SEAM + DEQUE MARKS.  Transcribed VERBATIM (WM 4335-4962).
                                ; MKGAP (BUF.MAC) reaches disk only here: MKROOM evicts a window edge (SPILL the
                                ; TXTBEG side to OUTFCB when scrolling forward, SPILLB the TXTEND side back to
                                ; the input/backup side when scrolling back).  UPDMARK keeps the three record
                                ; marks (OUTREC / SRCREC / BAKREC) that let PAGEOUT and PAGEBOT tell "already on
                                ; disk" from "must transfer", so nothing is written twice or lost.
                                ; PAGEDIR / PAGEWIN / PGNEED (scroll- and search-time paging) are real below:
                                ; PAGEDIR picks REWIND (backward, re-read spilled text) vs FILLBUF (forward),
                                ; and PGNEED / PAGEWIN keep PGMARGN bytes of text resident on the active edge.
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-20


                                ; The editor reaches them through BUF.MAC's PAGESTP and SCRLST (the line moves,
                                ; the line kill and the search sweep); PGBKTST drives PAGEDIR directly.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;PAGEDIR -- WM 4320: page more text into the window in the current scroll
                                ;direction -- REWIND (re-read text previously spilled to OUTFCB) when DIRFLG is
                                ;backward, else FILLBUF (read more of the input) when forward.
  0647'                         PAGEDIR:			; WM 4320
  0647'   CD 09E4'              	CALL	POLLBRK
  064A'   3A 0000*              	LDA	DIRFLG
  064D'   B7                    	ORA	A
  064E'   FA 0720'              	JM	REWIND
  0651'   C3 045E'              	JMP	FILLBUF
                                
                                ;MKROOM -- WM 4335: free gap space by evicting a window edge (DIRFLG picks).
  0654'                         MKROOM:				; WM 4335
  0654'   3A 0000*              	LDA	DIRFLG
  0657'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0658'   37                    	STC
  0659'   FC 0693'              	CM	SPILLB
  065C'   D0                    	RNC
  065D'   CD 031F'              	CALL	SPILL
  0660'   D0                    	RNC
  0661'   C3 0693'              	JMP	SPILLB
                                
                                ;PAGEWIN -- WM 4350: keep PGMARGN bytes of text buffered around the cursor on
                                ;the active edge (for a whole-file search); PAGEDIR one increment at a time
                                ;until PGNEED is satisfied or the source runs out.
  0664'                         PAGEWIN:			; WM 4350
  0664'   CD 0674'              	CALL	PGNEED
  0667'   D8                    	RC
  0668'   CD 0647'              	CALL	PAGEDIR
  066B'   D8                    	RC
  066C'   CD 0674'              	CALL	PGNEED
  066F'   D4 0647'              	CNC	PAGEDIR
  0672'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0673'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;PGNEED -- WM 4361: CY if the active edge (TXTBEG scanning back, GAPEND scanning
                                ;forward) is still within PGMARGN*256 bytes -- i.e. the resident text on that
                                ;side is shorter than the margin, so more must be paged in.  LHLD MARGLO reads
                                ;the word whose high byte is PGMARGN and whose low byte (MARGLO) is a fixed 0,
                                ;yielding PGMARGN*256 (WM does this as LHLD 272F).
  0674'                         PGNEED:				; WM 4361
  0674'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0675'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0676'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0677'   3A 0000*              	LDA	DIRFLG
  067A'   B7                    	ORA	A
  067B'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TXTBEG
  067E'   FA 0684'              	JM	PGNCMP
  0681'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,GAPEND
  0684'                         PGNCMP:				 ; WM 4371 -- span the active edge, compare to margin
  0684'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	MARGLO
  0687'   EB                    	XCHG
  0688'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PRSPAN
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-21


  068B'   60                    	MOV	H,B
  068C'   69                    	MOV	L,C
  068D'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  0690'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;SPILLB -- WM 4491: evict a batch of bottom (TXTEND-side) sectors via PAGEBOT.
  0693'                         SPILLB:				; WM 4491
  0693'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0694'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0695'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0696'   CD 06B3'              	CALL	PAGEBOT
  0699'   DA 0000*              	JC	POPRET
  069C'   3A 0000*              	LDA	IOBATCH
  069F'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  06A0'   05                    	DCR	B
  06A1'   87                    	ADD	A
  06A2'   4F                    	MOV	C,A
  06A3'   0D                    	DCR	C
  06A4'                         SPBLP:				; WM 4504 -- evict-batch loop
  06A4'   CD 06B3'              	CALL	PAGEBOT
  06A7'   05                    	DCR	B
  06A8'   CA 06AF'              	JZ	SPBDON
  06AB'   0D                    	DCR	C
  06AC'   C2 06A4'              	JNZ	SPBLP
  06AF'                         SPBDON:				 ; WM 4511
  06AF'   B7                    	ORA	A
  06B0'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;PAGEBOT -- WM 4520: evict the window's bottom sector back to the input side.
                                ;If it still aligns with the original, un-read the source (RECDEC); otherwise
                                ;write it to VIBACKUP$$$ -- SRCREC/BAKREC decide which.  Then TXTEND -= 128.
  06B3'                         PAGEBOT:			; WM 4520
  06B3'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  06B6'   CD 04BF'              	CALL	INRDY
  06B9'   C2 06CB'              	JNZ	PBSTEP
  06BC'   3A 0000*              	LDA	INLEN
  06BF'   57                    	MOV	D,A
  06C0'   CD 080B'              	CALL	SUBHA
  06C3'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  06C4'   7A                    	MOV	A,D
  06C5'   CD 03FC'              	CALL	STAGSEC
  06C8'   C3 06D0'              	JMP	PBRDLM
  06CB'                         PBSTEP:				 ; WM 4532 -- step back one sector at TXTEND
  06CB'   11 FF80               	LXI	D,0FF80H
  06CE'   19                    	DAD	D
  06CF'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  06D0'                         PBRDLM:				 ; WM 4537 -- check the read limit
  06D0'   E3                    	XTHL
  06D1'   CD 0638'              	CALL	CKRDLIM
  06D4'   E3                    	XTHL
  06D5'   D2 06DA'              	JNC	PBSRC
  06D8'   E1                    	POP	H
  06D9'   C9                    	RET
  06DA'                         PBSRC:				; WM 4545 -- read from the source if its rec is due
  06DA'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  06DB'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SRCREC
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-22


  06DE'   EB                    	XCHG
  06DF'   CD 07EC'              	CALL	RECBASE
  06E2'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  06E5'   E1                    	POP	H
  06E6'   D2 06F2'              	JNC	PBBAK
  06E9'   11 005C               	LXI	D,5CH
  06EC'   CD 096C'              	CALL	RECDEC
  06EF'   C3 0717'              	JMP	PBFIN
  06F2'                         PBBAK:				; WM 4557 -- else read / recycle from the backup
  06F2'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  06F3'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BAKREC
  06F6'   EB                    	XCHG
  06F7'   CD 07EC'              	CALL	RECBASE
  06FA'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  06FD'   E1                    	POP	H
  06FE'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,BAKFCB
  0701'   D2 070A'              	JNC	PBWBAK
  0704'   CD 0965'              	CALL	RECINC
  0707'   C3 0717'              	JMP	PBFIN
  070A'                         PBWBAK:				 ; WM 4569 -- write back a backup record; step BAKREC
  070A'   CD 095F'              	CALL	WRRECP
  070D'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  070E'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BAKREC
  0711'   2B                    	DCX	H
  0712'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BAKREC
  0715'   E1                    	POP	H
  0716'   04                    	INR	B
  0717'                         PBFIN:				; WM 4578 -- store new TXTEND; note input remaining
  0717'   CD 04BF'              	CALL	INRDY
  071A'   B7                    	ORA	A
  071B'   E1                    	POP	H
  071C'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TXTEND
  071F'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;REWIND -- WM 4755: scrolling back, re-read sectors previously spilled to
                                ;OUTFCB (by random record, stepping backward) and prepend them at TXTBEG.
                                ;Enabled only when OUTACT marks that text has actually been written out.
  0720'                         REWIND:				; WM 4755
  0720'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0721'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0722'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0723'   3A 0000*              	LDA	OUTACT
  0726'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0727'   37                    	STC
  0728'   CA 075B'              	JZ	RWNRET
  072B'   11 0693'              	LXI	D,SPILLB
  072E'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TXTBEG
  0731'   CD 04D9'              	CALL	RESVBUF
  0734'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
  0737'                         RWNLP:				; WM 4768 -- re-read one output record backward
  0737'   CD 09E4'              	CALL	POLLBRK
  073A'   11 FF80               	LXI	D,0FF80H
  073D'   19                    	DAD	D
  073E'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0741'   CD 075E'              	CALL	RWNREC		; DEVIATION 8: RDPREV, or from the source
  0744'   DA 075A'              	JC	RWNDON
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-23


  0747'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TXTBEG
  074A'   CD 0295'              	CALL	TLFSUB		; (appended) its line feeds are back in the
                                				;   window
  074D'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  074E'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	PGTOPM		; (appended) the window's top moved: 'u' reads
  0751'   23                    	INX	H		;   this to know its offsets have shifted
  0752'   22 0000*              	SHLD	PGTOPM
  0755'   E1                    	POP	H
  0756'   0D                    	DCR	C
  0757'   C2 0737'              	JNZ	RWNLP
  075A'                         RWNDON:				 ; WM 4779
  075A'   B7                    	ORA	A
  075B'                         RWNRET:				 ; WM 4782
  075B'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;RWNREC -- DEVIATION 8: RDPREV on OUTFCB (DE), except that a record below
                                ;SAMREC is the source's own, never written to name.$$$: it is read from the
                                ;source through SRCFCB and cleaned as FILLBUF cleans it.  HL = where.
  075E'                         RWNREC:
  075E'   CD 096C'              	CALL	RECDEC		; OUTPOS - 1
  0761'   D8                    	RC
  0762'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0763'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  0766'   EB                    	XCHG
  0767'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC
  076A'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff OUTPOS < SAMREC
  076D'   EB                    	XCHG
  076E'   D2 0786'              	JNC	RWNOUT
  0771'   22 0022*              	SHLD	SRCFCB+22H
  0774'   E1                    	POP	H
  0775'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SRCFCB
  0778'   CD 08DE'              	CALL	RDSEC
  077B'   D8                    	RC
  077C'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  077D'   CD 04A4'              	CALL	CLNSEC		; bit 7 off
  0780'   E1                    	POP	H
  0781'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0784'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0785'   C9                    	RET
  0786'   E1                    RWNOUT:	POP	H
  0787'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  078A'   C3 08DE'              	JMP	RDSEC
                                
                                ;MARKGB -- WM 4886: UPDMARK only when HL points at GAPBEG (falls into UPDMARK).
  078D'                         MARKGB:				; WM 4886
  078D'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  078E'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,GAPBEG
  0791'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  0794'   D1                    	POP	D
  0795'   C0                    	RNZ
                                ;UPDMARK -- WM 4898: after an edit, move the record marks that say which
                                ;records must be written again.  Each mark only ever moves one way here:
                                ;  OUTREC (TXTBEG/output side) is LOWERED to OUTPOS + the whole records from
                                ;  TXTBEG to GAPBEG, when that is lower (stored on CMP16's carry).  UPDMARK
                                ;  never raises it; only PAGEOUT (POFRSH) does.
                                ;  SRCREC and BAKREC (GAPEND/input side) are RAISED to RECBASE less the whole
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-24


                                ;  records from GAPEND to TXTEND, when that is not lower (stored on no carry).
                                ;CMP16 sets carry when DE < HL.  (The comment here used to say the opposite
                                ;for both sides -- issue #37.)
  0796'                         UPDMARK:			; WM 4898
  0796'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0797'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0798'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0799'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  079A'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TXTBEG
  079D'   CD 07FD'              	CALL	PTRREC
  07A0'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  07A3'   19                    	DAD	D
  07A4'   EB                    	XCHG
  07A5'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC		; DEVIATION 8: the source holds the text only
  07A8'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		;   up to the edit's record
  07AB'   D2 07B3'              	JNC	UMKSAM
  07AE'   EB                    	XCHG
  07AF'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SAMREC
  07B2'   EB                    	XCHG
  07B3'                         UMKSAM:
  07B3'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTREC
  07B6'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  07B9'   EB                    	XCHG
  07BA'   D2 07C0'              	JNC	UMKGAP
  07BD'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTREC
  07C0'                         UMKGAP:				 ; WM 4914 -- update the GAPEND-side marks
  07C0'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,GAPEND
  07C3'   CD 07FD'              	CALL	PTRREC
  07C6'   CD 07EC'              	CALL	RECBASE
  07C9'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  07CC'   EB                    	XCHG
  07CD'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SRCREC
  07D0'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  07D3'   EB                    	XCHG
  07D4'   DA 07DA'              	JC	UMKBAK
  07D7'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SRCREC
  07DA'                         UMKBAK:				 ; WM 4926 -- lower BAKREC if needed
  07DA'   EB                    	XCHG
  07DB'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BAKREC
  07DE'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  07E1'   EB                    	XCHG
  07E2'   DA 07E8'              	JC	UMKDON
  07E5'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BAKREC
  07E8'                         UMKDON:				 ; WM 4934
  07E8'   F1                    	POP	PSW
  07E9'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;RECBASE -- WM 4939: disk record base for the buffer (BAKPOS - source_rec + 7FFF).
                                ;7EH is the source FCB's random-record word (FCB 005C + 22H).
  07EC'                         RECBASE:			; WM 4939
  07EC'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  07ED'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BAKPOS
  07F0'   EB                    	XCHG
  07F1'   2A 007E               	LHLD	7EH
  07F4'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  07F7'   11 7FFF               	LXI	D,7FFFH
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-25


  07FA'   19                    	DAD	D
  07FB'   D1                    	POP	D
  07FC'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;PTRREC -- WM 4951: DE = record number (128-byte) for the pointer pair at HL.
  07FD'                         PTRREC:				; WM 4951
  07FD'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PRSPAN
  0800'   60                    	MOV	H,B
  0801'   69                    	MOV	L,C
  0802'   29                    	DAD	H
  0803'   5C                    	MOV	E,H
  0804'   16 00                 	MVI	D,0H
  0806'   D2 080A'              	JNC	PTRRET
  0809'   14                    	INR	D
  080A'                         PTRRET:				 ; WM 4961
  080A'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;SUBHA -- WM 2066: HL := HL - A.
  080B'                         SUBHA:				; WM 2066
  080B'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  080C'   67                    	MOV	H,A
  080D'   7D                    	MOV	A,L
  080E'   94                    	SUB	H
  080F'   E1                    	POP	H
  0810'   6F                    	MOV	L,A
  0811'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  0812'   DE 00                 	SBI	0H
  0814'   67                    	MOV	H,A
  0815'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; BDOS GLUE -- WM 5396-5424.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;BDOSFN -- WM 5396: set DMA=80H, then fall into BDOSC for the inline fn.
  0816'                         BDOSFN:				; WM 5396
  0816'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0817'   11 0080               	LXI	D,80H
  081A'   CD 081F'              	CALL	BDOSC
  081D'   1A                    	DB	1AH
  081E'   D1                    	POP	D
                                ;BDOSC -- WM 5412: BDOS call with the fn number stored inline after the CALL.
  081F'                         BDOSC:				; WM 5412
  081F'   E3                    	XTHL
  0820'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0821'   4E                    	MOV	C,M
  0822'   23                    	INX	H
  0823'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0824'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0825'   CD 0005               	CALL	5H
  0828'   E1                    	POP	H
  0829'   D1                    	POP	D
  082A'   C1                    	POP	B
  082B'   E3                    	XTHL
  082C'   C9                    	RET
                                
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-26


                                ;FATAL -- WM 5429 (deviation 2): share ERRMSG's tail.
  082D'                         FATAL:				; WM 5429
  082D'   C3 0000*              	JMP	ERRMSG
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; FILE PRIMITIVES -- WM 5436-5566.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;OPENF -- WM 5438: BDOS-open the FCB at DE, then zero its random-record bytes.
  0830'                         OPENF:				; WM 5438
  0830'   CD 0816'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  0833'   0F                    	DB	0FH
  0834'   3C                    	INR	A
  0835'                         ZERORR:				; WM 5444 -- zero FCB+22H/+23H
  0835'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0836'   21 0023               	LXI	H,23H
  0839'   19                    	DAD	D
  083A'   36 00                 	MVI	M,0H
  083C'   2B                    	DCX	H
  083D'   36 00                 	MVI	M,0H
  083F'   E1                    	POP	H
  0840'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;CLSBAK/CLOSEC -- WM 5455/5459: close the FCB at DE if its open flag is set.
  0841'                         CLSBAK:				; WM 5455
  0841'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,BAKFCB
  0844'                         CLOSEC:				; WM 5459
  0844'   1B                    	DCX	D
  0845'   1B                    	DCX	D
  0846'   1A                    	LDAX	D
  0847'   13                    	INX	D
  0848'   13                    	INX	D
  0849'   B7                    	ORA	A
  084A'   C8                    	RZ
                                ;CLOSEF -- WM 5469: BDOS-close the file; FATAL 'CLOSE ERR' on failure.
  084B'                         CLOSEF:				; WM 5469
  084B'   CD 0816'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  084E'   10                    	DB	10H
  084F'   3C                    	INR	A
  0850'   C0                    	RNZ
  0851'   CD 082D'              	CALL	FATAL
  0854'   43 4C 4F 53           	DB	'CLOSE ERR',0H
  0858'   45 20 45 52           
  085C'   52 00                 
                                
                                ;KILLBAK -- WM 5478: close then delete VIBACKUP$$$ (BAKFCB).
  085E'                         KILLBAK:			; WM 5478
  085E'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,BAKFCB
  0861'   CD 0844'              	CALL	CLOSEC
                                ;DELF -- WM 5483: BDOS-delete the file named by the FCB at DE.
  0864'                         DELF:				; WM 5483
  0864'   CD 0816'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  0867'   13                    	DB	13H
  0868'   1B                    	DCX	D
  0869'   CD 08EF'              	CALL	IOEOF
  086C'   13                    	INX	D
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-27


  086D'   C3 08EF'              	JMP	IOEOF
                                
                                ;DELRST -- WM 5492: delete the FCB's file, then ZERORR (prep a fresh file).
  0870'                         DELRST:				; WM 5492
  0870'   CD 0864'              	CALL	DELF
  0873'   CD 0835'              	CALL	ZERORR
                                ;MAKEF -- WM 5497: BDOS-create the file; FATAL 'DIRECTORY FULL' on failure.
  0876'                         MAKEF:				; WM 5497
  0876'   CD 0816'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  0879'   16                    	DB	16H
  087A'   3C                    	INR	A
  087B'   C0                    	RNZ
  087C'                         DIRFUL:				 ; WM 5503
  087C'   CD 082D'              	CALL	FATAL
  087F'   44 49 52 45           	DB	'DIRECTORY FULL',0H
  0883'   43 54 4F 52           
  0887'   59 20 46 55           
  088B'   4C 4C 00              
                                
                                ;RENAME -- WM 5534: rename the file on the FCB at DE to the 3-byte type at HL.
  088E'                         RENAME:				; WM 5534
  088E'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  088F'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0890'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0891'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0892'   21 0010               	LXI	H,10H
  0895'   19                    	DAD	D
  0896'   01 0010               	LXI	B,10H
  0899'   EB                    	XCHG
  089A'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY
  089D'   36 00                 	MVI	M,0H
  089F'   D1                    	POP	D
  08A0'   21 0019               	LXI	H,19H
  08A3'   19                    	DAD	D
  08A4'   EB                    	XCHG
  08A5'   E1                    	POP	H
  08A6'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  08A7'   CD 08CD'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  08AA'   E1                    	POP	H
  08AB'   D1                    	POP	D
  08AC'   C1                    	POP	B
                                ;RENF -- WM 5557: BDOS-rename; FATAL 'RENAME FAILURE' (CP/M-1 only) on failure.
  08AD'                         RENF:				; WM 5557
  08AD'   CD 0816'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  08B0'   17                    	DB	17H
  08B1'   3C                    	INR	A
  08B2'   C0                    	RNZ
  08B3'   3A 09F8'              	LDA	CPMNEW
  08B6'   B7                    	ORA	A
  08B7'   C0                    	RNZ
  08B8'   CD 082D'              	CALL	FATAL
  08BB'   52 45 4E 41           	DB	'RENAME FAILURE',0H
  08BF'   4D 45 20 46           
  08C3'   41 49 4C 55           
  08C7'   52 45 00              
                                
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-28


                                ;CPYBAK/CPYTYP -- WM 5178/5182: copy a 3-byte file type from [HL] to [DE].
  08CA'                         CPYBAK:				; WM 5178
  08CA'   21 09F5'              	LXI	H,BAKEXT
  08CD'                         CPYTYP:				; WM 5182
  08CD'   01 0003               	LXI	B,3H
  08D0'   C3 0000*              	JMP	MEMCPY
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; RANDOM-RECORD ENGINE -- WM 5568-5789.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;RDNEXT -- WM 5569: RDSEC, then advance the record number.
  08D3'                         RDNEXT:				; WM 5569
  08D3'   CD 08DE'              	CALL	RDSEC
  08D6'   D4 0965'              	CNC	RECINC
  08D9'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;RDPREV -- WM 5575: step the record number back, then RDSEC.
  08DA'                         RDPREV:				; WM 5575
  08DA'   CD 096C'              	CALL	RECDEC
  08DD'   D8                    	RC
                                ;RDSEC -- WM 5588: read one record into [HL] (CY on EOF).
  08DE'                         RDSEC:				; WM 5588
  08DE'   CD 0000*              	CALL	KBPOLL		; WM: CALL GETKEY
  08E1'   AF                    	XRA	A
  08E2'   CD 0997'              	CALL	SETREC
  08E5'   DA 08EF'              	JC	IOEOF
  08E8'   CD 081F'              	CALL	BDOSC
  08EB'   14                    	DB	14H
  08EC'   B7                    	ORA	A
  08ED'   3D                    	DCR	A
  08EE'   C0                    	RNZ
                                ;IOEOF -- WM 5600: mark an I/O read as EOF (zero count, set carry).
  08EF'                         IOEOF:				; WM 5600
  08EF'   1B                    	DCX	D
  08F0'   AF                    	XRA	A
  08F1'   12                    	STAX	D
  08F2'   13                    	INX	D
  08F3'   37                    	STC
  08F4'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;WRREC -- WM 5609: write one record with extent / DISK FULL handling.
  08F5'                         WRREC:				; WM 5609
  08F5'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  08F6'   62                    	MOV	H,D
  08F7'   6B                    	MOV	L,E
  08F8'   2B                    	DCX	H
  08F9'   2B                    	DCX	H
  08FA'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  08FB'   B7                    	ORA	A
  08FC'   CC 0939'              	CZ	WRMAKE		; DEVIATION 9: WM is CZ DELRST
  08FF'   36 FF                 	MVI	M,0FFH
  0901'   3E FF                 	MVI	A,0FFH
  0903'   32 0000*              	STA	WRKMAD		; APPENDED: a work file exists -> DISCRD must run
  0906'   E1                    	POP	H
  0907'   CD 094F'              	CALL	WRSEC
